Beware: Rabbits                NannyMUD Times                        Page 14

  Beware the brewing danger!

  Summon all your courage, dear reader, for the story I am about to reveal
  is indeed very troubling to the mind. This is a tale of beasts,
  deceiving in their seeming innocence, but foreboding a terrible danger.

  A tale of Rabbits.

  Even while traveling in the Blanka's newbie town have I noticed these
  treacherous creatures, holding tightly to their carrots, but I never felt
  anything was wrong. Only later, meeting yet the same specimen in Greece,
  then in Anvil's beginner-world, and even right here near the green,
  had sparked some suspicion.

  Suddenly, it dawned on me. There were FIVE of them! Of course! The beasts'
  single but effective weapon is their multiplication! A weird but sure
  way to overcome the world! I killed off the beasts and proceeded in my
  search.

  This cunning plan was painfully clear to me, but I wanted to get some
  evidence. And it didn't delay to come: the Bunny MMDCCCXLVI in the quarry!
  It seems like they have had quite a bit of success there!

  Another evidence came to me the next night. In my dream, I was rummaging
  through old scrolls belonging to a great magician called Fibonacci.
  A great deal of his research was about rabbits; I was reading one of
  the scrolls when suddenly the Master appeared in a flash of lightning:
  "WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE, PETTY SPY?!?"

  I woke up, stricken by terror. Next to me, I found a charred scroll.
  It was almost unreadable; all I could make out is the following:

      1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, #############
      ### 144, 233, 377, 610, 987,#######
      #########4181, 6765, 10946, 177####
      ##################8, 75025, 121393,
      ##########################, 832040,
      ###################################
      ###################################

  I was mesmerized by the endless sequence of numbers. The comma after the
  last one gave me the creeps.

  That should not happen! I shall kill them all! I urge you, dear reader,
  to finish off the Rabbit next time you walk by, for ignoring this danger
  is a sure way to Rabbit domination over the whole world! Only together
  will we manage to thwart their dreadful plan.
  
  -Liozar
